        <p>From Dr. D. J. BOULTON AND Co., Horricastle. We have made pretty extensive use of Chlorodyne Inoue practice lately and look upon it as an excellent direct Seda- tive and Anti-spasmodic. It seems to allay pain and irrita- tion in whatever organ, and from whatever cause. It I nduCes a feeling of comfort and quietrcie not obtainable by any oLher remedy, and it seems to possess ,this great advantage over all other sedatives ; thst it leaves no unpleasant after effects. " Earl Russell communicated to the College of Physicians that he received a despatch from her Majeity's Consul at Manilla to the effect that Cholera had bien raging fearfully, and that the ONLY remedy of any service was CHLORO- DYNE."—See Lancet, Ist December, 1864.</p>
