      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-12-02_WidnesExaminer_art0078" n="art0078">
        <head>LATEST NEWS.</head>
        <p>LATEST NEWS.</p>
        <p>THE RAILWAY SMASH. AT CREWE. INQUEST ON THE TWO DRIVERS. The inquiry by Mr. Coroner Yates into the circum- stances attending the death of William Lovett, of Staf- ford, and John Henry Yates, of Wavertree' engiue drivers in the employ of the London and North-Western Railway Company, who were killed in the railway col- lision near Crewe on the 19th ult., was r..surned at Crewe yesterday morning. THu vERDICT : IMPORTANT REDO .d dE The jury, after some deliberation, returned a verdict that the men met their death thrdugh misadventure, add.ng that in their opinion Lovett was going too fast. The jury also handed to the Coroner the following riders: ! —This jury desires to place on record their admiration of the conduct ot Signalman William Graham, who, witn great presence of mind and with great forethought seeing the mail train approaching rapidly, placed the signals of the fast down line at danger, thereby bringing the train to a standstill in time to prevent what inns: in their opinion have been a most terrible calamity. The seccnd rider was as lellJw3 i--The jary further recom- mend for the considelation of the OffiCiell3 of the com- pany the desirability if practicaole of so placing tha signals as to make it an impossibility for the signals of the fast and slow lines to to mistaken for &amp;mu other by the drivers of trains, of devising some means, mechani- cal or otherwise, by which the driver of a train could be made aware that the distaht signal of the line on which he was proce'ding was at danger, if such were the case.</p>
        <p>LATEST LOCAL WEATHER FORECAST. The weather report for the North-west of England up to noon to-say is as follows :—Wesculy strong winds and gales ; squally ; some rain. A COAIIIERCIA.L TRAVELLER KILLED IN THE STREETS. Yesterday afternoon, while a traveller in the employ of a Liverpool firm was passing a provision warehouse he was struck on the shoulder by a box of bacon in a sling, and knocked into the basement, twenty feet deOp. He fractured his skull and died immediately. A GIRL BURNT TO DEATH.</p>
        <p>-- - A fire broke out in a grocer's shop at Airdrie, yester- day morniog, and resalted in tho death ot Ellen Walker, a little girl, twelve years of age. Her father and mother and the other memb3rs of the family had narrow escapes. WRECK OF A. BRITISH SHIP.</p>
        <p>_ A despatch from St. John's, Newfoundland, states that the British steamer Scottish King, of Sunderland, has been completely wrecked on the coast during a thick fog. The ct=v,- w—e saved. THE AUSTRIAN EMPERO JUBILEE. A GENERAL AMNESIA'.</p>
        <p>VIENNA, THCrESDAY„ The official " Weiner Zeitung " to-day publishes an autograph letter from the Emperor Francis Joserh to the Minister of Justice, in which fits Majesty, on the occa- sion of his jubilee, grants a full amnesty to all parsons who have been guilty of the c:ime of less majeste, or may have offended members of the Imperial Family. Five hundred and forty-eight persons condemned to various terms of imprisonment for ocher offences have the remainder of their sentences remitted. FALL OF I HIGH CHIIINEY. BRIDGEWATER CANAL BLOCKED. About three o'clock yeat‘irdav morning a strong wind caused a chimney at Bedford Foundry. Leigh, 120 feet high, to collapse. It was blown from its foundations, and fell right across the Ship Canal Company's Bridge- water Canal, smashing the telegraph wires, poles, and hedge. Thousands of uricks fell into the canal, comple- tely stopping the loaded boats. At 9.30 traffic had not been resumed. The estimated damage is £3OO. THE GORDON MENIORIAL SCHIt:ME. Up to Wedne, day night the Sirdar had a promise of £40,000 for his scheme.</p>
        <p>EXPIRATION OF TENANCY. RELINQUISHING THE BUSINESS. CLEARANCE SALE. JOHN S. GREEN. BOOKSELLER, STATIONER, ETC., 34, BRIDGE-STREET. WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>In terminating his tenancy is also relinquishing the above- mentioned BUSINESS, and has decided to offer the whole of his</p>
