      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1898-12-02_WidnesExaminer_art0079" n="art0079">
        <head>ANNUAL MEETING OF THE WARRINGTON SWIMMING CLUB.</head>
        <p>ANNUAL MEETING OF THE WAR- RINGTON SWIMMING CLUB.</p>
        <p>On M-mday evening at the Corporation Baths, the Warrington Swimming Club held their annual meeting. Mr. 0. H. Wood occupied the chair. more was a fair number of members present including Dr. Cannell (President of the Club). The annual report givea in our last issue,and balance sheet were adopted. The CHAIRMAN in proposing the re-election of Coun- cillor Dr. Canted as president said they woutd not accept any refusal. (Hear, hear.) He had been a great friend to the club, having tskeE their part on many occasions and fought many battles for them. He con- sidered Dr. Gannett was the best man they could have. (Applause.) The motion was unanimously carried and Councillor Dr. Cancel, in reply, said he would cerrainly do his best for the Club, bat he really considered a change was desirable and it was good to have new blood. The following were elected vice-presidents :—The members of the Town Hall, Park, and Baths Committee, dr R Pierpoint, M.P., Alderman 11 Roberts, J.P., Coun- cillor „W Pierpoint, J.P., Councillor John Evans, and Messrs 11 Asil.ton, A H Croefield, Percy Davies, W J For- shaw, John Houghton, Luke Talbot, H Thornton, El 'raft, Fairfield Turner, J C Parr, R A Naylor. The other elections resulted a follows :—Captain of club, T L'cker ; 'captain pole team, W Ashton; sub- captain,A. G Robertson; hon. treasurer,C H Wood ; hon. secretary, F Garaide ; joint ban secretary, A. G Robert- son • auditors, Messrs. Hardy and Taylor ; deleoate to Northern Counties A S A, T Locker. ; committee, Messrs W Ashton, Ruck, Creighton, Bailey, Harding, Sherlock, Taylor, Grey, Critchley, lkseow, A Astton, and 8 Bea- man.</p>
        <p>OFFRE, Councillor Dr. CAVNELL stated that the Town Hall, , Park, and Baths Committee would be prepared to give two sea Son tickets t- aia7 gentleman who would undez.. take to teach swimming in the baths at a reasonable charge. Wo,kingmen had to pay too much at present. ' The money thus acquired could go either to those who taught or to the fut. di of the clue. The President was thanked, and the consideration of the matter referred to the committee. vote of thetas to the Chairman concluded the meeting.</p>
        <p>..—........--.. A LOCAL PATEXTEL—The following patent amongst °theta Was applied for and pubben€d in tits " Official Journal of Patents" during the weak ending November 191 h, 1698. No. 23,931, U. 0. Bennett and the Hope and like articles." "improvemente on clFoundrycloset C0.,4a Limited,nodv ia a tWo ra; bri ni ag tcokn. fort LAMPS. Oil Stoves. Coke Stores, Braes Fenders. Largest selection.—J. S. GARLAND, Ironmonger, Bridge- street. Warrington. FOR RVRNING WEAR, Latest Novelties in Silks. Alpacas. Nun's Veilings, Fans, laleves,and Feather Boas. W. T. WILLIAMS, Sankey-street,Legn-street.Warrington. 411,</p>
