        <head>"Look before you Leap."</head>
        <p>"Look before you Leap."</p>
        <p>Leaping is always more or less a dangerous busi- ness, and requires a wise man to do the thing properly. As for myself, leaping is not much in my Lisa; I prefer walking, or at most running or biking ; but if some folks prefer leaping, I have no objection. I only offer this bit of advice, "Look before you leap." Before you spend your hard- earned money in medicines be sure the remedy is genuine. Page WOODCOCK'S Wind Pills were intro- duced to the British public 47 years ago, and ever since they have been gaining increased confidence as the finest remedy in the world for the cure of Indigestion, Liver Complaints, Wind on the Stomach, Costiveness, Sick Headache, Nervous Debility, Palpitation of the Heart, Biliousness, &amp;e. Mr. W. H. Parsons, of 4, Crescent-road, Clap- ham, S.W., June, 1393, vrites ;—" I have been a great sufferer from INDIGESTION, &amp;a. Have tried a great many remedies, but found none to , equal your WIND PILLS, which have worked magic upon me. Trusting that many others may find the boon of them. You may make what use you like of this,. It is a fact Page Woodcock's Wind Pills being purely Vege- table, Tasteless, and Mild and Tonic in their action, may be taken with perfect Way by the most delicate of either sea. Page Woodcock's Wind Pills are sold by al Medicine Vendors at is. Id., and 23. 9d., or are sent free for pries by Page Woodcock, Lincoln. Be particular that you ask for " Page Wood- cock's Wind Pills," and see Wit you get no other.</p>
