        <p>GREAT STOCKTAK IN G SALE AT PITTS'S LONDON-ROAD, MANCHESTER. (Just past Station through Railway Arch.) THOUSANDS OF POUNDS WORTH BEING CLEARED OUT TOTALLY IRRESPECTIVE OF PROFIT. DITTS'S STOCKTAKING SALE HAS COMMENCED. , 1 This important announcement will doubtless send a thrill of pleasure through the shrewd public who always make a point of patronising Pates ,Sales, knowing full well that at such times a sav:ng of 25 to 50 per cent may often be effected. Pitts's are renowned far and wide, in fact stand preeminent for always givinz UTMOST POSSIBLE VALUE, but at their Stocktaking Sales Pitt', give MORE THAN VALUE as in many instances articles are marked CONSIDERABLY isELOW COST, in order to clear them out to facilitate Stocktaking. PITTS'S believe that if they sacrifice several hundred pounds. during this great bale, giving their customers the. benefit such sacrifice will pay them in the long run as an advertisement by still further strengthening their well- known reputation as the BEST and CHEAPEST GENERAL FURNISHERS. It is utterly impossible for anyone, not having favoured Pitts's with a visit, to conceive the astound- ing variety and magnitude of Pitts's UNRIVALLED STOCK of new and second-hand FURNITURE, BEDSTEADS, PIANOS, CYCLES. EASSINETTES, eta., eta.. La fact every household and office requisite, much of which Pitts's have secured at about a third of original cost from numerous large residences the reuses of which have already been advertised. Pittee intend this sale to far surpass all previous efforts. As such an opportunity as this of economical fur- nishing occurs but seldom it is the BOUNDEN DUTY of everyone desirous of laying out theirlhard-earned money to the BEST ADVANTAGE to call at PITTS'S WITHOUT DE- LAY, or they may be too late. TIEITTS'S HOUSES OF FURNITURE at 14,2428/, 34,50 ▪ 75, 100, up to 1,000 guineas need no praise; one might as well paint the lily or gild refined gold. During the sale, Pitts's will not alter th-s prises, but instead augment the quantity and quality of the articles, so you may take it for granted that each House of Furniture is worth DOUBLE , THE PRICE ASKED. Inspection 'will verify this state- , ment. PI ITS/ , guineas, worth £35 ; includes a Splendid serviceable , suite in leather, dining table, fender and brasses complete, capital Brussels carpet, with hearihrug to match, window fittings. An. Kitchen includes strong Windsor chairs, strong table with heavy white top, nine yanis of seasoned oilcloth, bearthrug, fender and irons complete. Bedroom has all re- quisite articles ; massive bedstead, mattresses, bed bolster, l and two pillows (guaranteed new and clean), carpet, toilet ware U., all complete and full size. "PITTS N ENTIRE CONTENTS OF SEVEN-ROOMED I • HOUSE, originally cost £lBO for 75 guineas. The I dining-room is In morocco leather, the drawing-room Is in rosewood, a spare room upstairs fitted as a smoke-room is in saddlebags. Furniture for kitehen, hall, stairs, landing, cellars, A. The first bedroom is in American walnut, Incl ding wardrobe, dressing-table, washstand, chairs, Ac., bedsteads, bedding, carpet, rug, and toilet service. The second bedroom is in ash, and the third bedroom is in mahogany, Undoubtedly the greatest bargain ever offered. UNTTS'S STOCKTAKING. CARPET BARGAINS. 1 Largest and best selected Stock of Brussels, Tapestry, Axminster, Wilton, Velvet Pile, etc., etc. Linoleum, Floor- cloths, etch All English manufacture, at exceptionally low prices to clear. Fitted free of charge by competent men. PITTS'S STOCKTAKING. PIANOS, CYCLES, HAS- SINETTES. LAMPS, CHINA, EARTHENWARE, PICTURES, ENGRAVINGS, CUTLERY, and OTHER BARGAINS too numerous to mention. Exceptional value. PITTS'S STOCKTAKING. OFFICE AND LIBRARY BARGAINS. —For Half a Century the word" Pitta's ' and Good Office Furniture have been synonymous. Pitta's have either the same article at a less price than any other firm, or a better article at the canoe price. Desks, Tables, Chairs, Stools. Book